sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Keys as authorized_keys
    participant Pair as whip-pair
    actor User
    participant Whip as Whip client

    Pair->>Pair: Bind selected interface
    Pair->>Pair: Generate token and ephemeral TLS certificate
    Pair-->>User: Show one-time WP3 QR code
    User->>Whip: Scan QR code
    Note over Pair,Whip: QR bootstrap: endpoint + token + certificate pin
    Whip->>Whip: Decode endpoint, token, and certificate pin
    Whip->>Pair: Connect with TLS and verify certificate SHA-256
    Whip->>Pair: PairingHello { token }
    Pair->>Pair: Check token and server-side expiry
    Pair-->>Whip: PairingServerInfo { SSH profile + host-key fingerprint }
    Whip->>Pair: EnrollmentRequest { device name + OpenSSH public key }
    Pair->>Pair: Validate key and calculate fingerprint
    Pair-->>User: Show device and key fingerprint
    User->>Pair: Approve or reject
    alt User approves before expiry
        Pair->>Keys: Append key safely and idempotently
        Keys-->>Pair: Added or already present
        Pair-->>Whip: approved { fingerprint, already_present }
        Pair->>Pair: Stop one-shot server
    else User rejects
        Pair-->>Whip: rejected { code, message }
        Pair->>Pair: Continue listening until success or expiry
    end
